# Git workflow (features → PR)

When starting **new feature work**, create a feature branch **before** writing code.

## Branch naming

- Pattern: `{type}/{feature-name}` (kebab-case)
- Types: `feat/`, `fix/`, `refactor/`, `docs/`, `chore/`
- Examples: `feat/video-forge-editor`, `fix/audio-overlay-preview`

## Steps

1. `git checkout main && git pull`
2. `git checkout -b feat/<feature-name>` (pick the right type prefix)
3. Implement and commit on this branch (only when the user asks to commit)
4. When ready: `git push -u origin HEAD` and open a PR against `main`

## Skip branching when

- Read-only questions or exploration
- Continuing work on an existing feature branch
- User explicitly says to use `main` or a named branch

